1
00:01:41,340 --> 00:01:43,280
Anger of Coexistence

2
00:01:45,920 --> 00:01:48,680
What? A present for Chief Ohara?

3
00:01:49,420 --> 00:01:53,440
He's receiving a 35-year
service commendation soon.

4
00:01:53,440 --> 00:01:56,620
So we decided to give him some kind of gift.

5
00:01:56,620 --> 00:01:58,220
What do you think would be good?

6
00:01:58,620 --> 00:01:59,480
Obviously.

7
00:01:59,480 --> 00:02:00,940
Cash, of course.

8
00:02:00,940 --> 00:02:03,080
Nothing beats cash as a present.

9
00:02:03,080 --> 00:02:06,520
But something more
memorable would be better.

10
00:02:06,520 --> 00:02:12,040
I remember every New Year's money
amount I've received since I was five!

11
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:14,380
That's just something mass-produced.

12
00:02:14,380 --> 00:02:17,840
After all, something that
leaves a physical mark is better.

13
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:19,000
Do you think so?

14
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:21,420
Hey, how about a bronze statue?

15
00:02:21,420 --> 00:02:22,560
A bronze statue?

16
00:02:24,580 --> 00:02:29,300
No way, no way. A middle-aged
man's bare body is just creepy.

17
00:02:29,300 --> 00:02:31,220
It's not a nude, senpai.

18
00:02:31,220 --> 00:02:32,860
It's a bust, a bust.

19
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:35,440
That kind of thing.

20
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:40,760
Just imagining a person
posing naked is creepy.

21
00:02:40,760 --> 00:02:43,760
Where would you even
display something like that?

22
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:46,680
Hey, let's secretly make
a bronze statue right now

23
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:49,780
and surprise him by giving it
to him on the award ceremony day.

24
00:02:49,780 --> 00:02:50,580
Sounds good.

25
00:02:50,580 --> 00:02:54,260
Wait, we can't make this
without the man's cooperation.

26
00:02:54,260 --> 00:02:55,500
Really? Is that so?

27
00:02:55,500 --> 00:03:01,360
I think you insert a straw into the nose, harden
it with plaster, and then take a mold from that.

28
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:03,840
Then we'll have to do it
secretly while he's sleeping.

29
00:03:04,380 --> 00:03:06,660
That's how you make a life mask, though.

30
00:03:07,240 --> 00:03:10,880
It says they can make it
if we send a few photos.

31
00:03:10,880 --> 00:03:12,260
Is that right?

32
00:03:12,700 --> 00:03:14,680
Then let's go place the order right away.

33
00:03:14,680 --> 00:03:15,420
Yeah, let's.

34
00:03:15,420 --> 00:03:16,240
Wait, wait.

35
00:03:16,240 --> 00:03:20,960
I could make it without even looking
at the Chief's face in a photo!

36
00:03:20,960 --> 00:03:23,680
I could even make it cheap for you.

37
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:24,380
No way.

38
00:03:24,380 --> 00:03:26,420
It's not like building a model kit.

39
00:03:26,420 --> 00:03:29,360
Besides, until now we've always just
left it to the seniors like that.

40
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:30,800
Have you ever once done it properly?

41
00:03:31,140 --> 00:03:33,220
Leaving it to a professional is best.

42
00:03:34,540 --> 00:03:37,460
Damn, you both rejected it in stereo!

43
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:40,240
Isn't this photo a good one?

44
00:03:40,860 --> 00:03:42,020
Nice expression.

45
00:03:42,020 --> 00:03:44,240
That one really looks like Chief Ohara.

46
00:03:44,240 --> 00:03:46,280
This one looks even more like the Chief!

47
00:03:46,280 --> 00:03:47,280
See?

48
00:03:47,780 --> 00:03:52,020
Isn't this the series of angry photos
of the Chief that Senpai took before?

49
00:03:52,020 --> 00:03:53,740
No way, not these.

50
00:03:53,740 --> 00:03:56,880
His angry face is the most like the Chief,
isn't it?

51
00:03:57,400 --> 00:04:00,740
That's because Senpai is
always the one getting scolded.

52
00:04:00,740 --> 00:04:03,320
The Chief is normally so gentle, you know.

53
00:04:03,840 --> 00:04:04,920
Is this one no good?

54
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:07,540
Then this photo it is.

55
00:04:07,540 --> 00:04:08,520
Settled, then.

56
00:04:08,520 --> 00:04:11,300
I mean, this photo's better, right?

57
00:04:11,880 --> 00:04:12,860
You're being so persistent, aren't you?

58
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:19,460
Understood, we'll take on the job.

59
00:04:21,400 --> 00:04:24,480
Did you bring a photo of the gentleman?

60
00:04:24,480 --> 00:04:26,740
Yes, will this one do?

61
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:28,540
Yeah, that's fine.

62
00:04:29,260 --> 00:04:30,960
Then input this one.

63
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:31,680
Yes.

64
00:04:32,540 --> 00:04:34,180
Input it?

65
00:04:34,900 --> 00:04:41,520
At this workshop, we use the photo to form
the original model with 3D computer graphics.

66
00:04:41,520 --> 00:04:44,440
Wow, it's pretty high-tech

67
00:04:47,820 --> 00:04:49,780
It's already done? That's amazing.

68
00:04:49,780 --> 00:04:53,960
It's realistic. Is this okay? Like this?

69
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:59,840
Well, maybe we should tighten
up the mouth a little more.

70
00:05:01,680 --> 00:05:03,060
It has a police officer's look, doesn't it.

71
00:05:03,060 --> 00:05:04,160
Like this, then.

72
00:05:09,220 --> 00:05:10,500
Yes, yes, that's the feeling exactly.

73
00:05:10,500 --> 00:05:12,620
It really captures the Chief's character.

74
00:05:12,620 --> 00:05:15,400
There's kindness mixed
in with the sternness.

75
00:05:15,400 --> 00:05:17,280
Then we'll go with this one, please.

76
00:05:17,780 --> 00:05:18,600
Understood.

77
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:20,440
This looks like fun.

78
00:05:20,440 --> 00:05:22,900
Try out a few more variations.

79
00:05:23,640 --> 00:05:24,020
Yes.

80
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:26,080
Ryo-chan, you're hopeless.

81
00:05:26,520 --> 00:05:28,640
Senpai loves anything new.

82
00:05:30,520 --> 00:05:32,920
It'll be finished in about two weeks.

83
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:33,840
Got it.

84
00:05:34,420 --> 00:05:36,060
Senpai, we're heading home.

85
00:05:36,060 --> 00:05:37,560
Go on ahead without me.

86
00:05:37,560 --> 00:05:40,020
I'll stay and watch a bit
longer before going home.

87
00:05:41,500 --> 00:05:44,020
Ryo-chan, don't get in the way too much.

88
00:05:44,020 --> 00:05:45,160
I know, I know.

89
00:05:47,340 --> 00:05:50,840
But busts all have the same expression,
don't they?

90
00:05:50,840 --> 00:05:53,680
They're too serious and lack any fun.

91
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:56,920
They're usually commemorative gifts,
so it can't be helped.

92
00:05:58,640 --> 00:06:00,700
Don't you want to make
something a little different?

93
00:06:00,960 --> 00:06:03,240
Well, I wouldn't say I don't, but...

94
00:06:03,640 --> 00:06:06,140
Don't you want to make
an expression like this?

95
00:06:06,460 --> 00:06:07,960
It's certainly interesting.

96
00:06:07,960 --> 00:06:10,860
I've never made a bust with
an expression like this.

97
00:06:10,860 --> 00:06:13,200
Right? Even a pro would think so,
wouldn't they?

98
00:06:13,200 --> 00:06:16,440
I insisted that this
photo was the better one.

99
00:06:17,060 --> 00:06:17,860
Is that so?

100
00:06:17,980 --> 00:06:18,340
It is.

101
00:06:18,340 --> 00:06:20,940
Let's make the bust using this photo.

102
00:06:20,940 --> 00:06:23,540
But what about the earlier request?

103
00:06:23,540 --> 00:06:27,100
This one better captures
the Chief's true character.

104
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:35,740
Sure. But you said it was interesting, that you wanted to make something like this.
If you said that, then that would be

105
00:06:35,740 --> 00:06:48,840
an artist, wouldn't it? Making boring stuff like this all the time and being satisfied with it?
But this is work, making things to order. Where did your pride as an artist go?

106
00:06:49,960 --> 00:06:53,680
That blazing passion for
creativity has vanished

107
00:06:54,800 --> 00:07:12,960
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu

108
00:07:12,960 --> 00:07:14,260
As expected of a pro.

109
00:07:14,260 --> 00:07:15,540
Right, right.

110
00:07:15,540 --> 00:07:17,360
While we're at it,
let's change the clothes too.

111
00:07:17,360 --> 00:07:18,920
How about this one?

112
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:21,100
You've got good taste.

113
00:07:21,100 --> 00:07:23,040
Then that, and the hat too.

114
00:07:24,080 --> 00:07:24,960
Perfect.

115
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:28,380
It's already finished?

116
00:07:28,920 --> 00:07:30,940
It's only been three days, you know.

117
00:07:30,940 --> 00:07:33,020
You know,
they really got into the spirit of it.

118
00:07:33,020 --> 00:07:35,360
They put it together in no time at all.

119
00:07:36,860 --> 00:07:39,340
It's a superb piece, take a look.

120
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:47,700
This is Chief Ohara, right?

121
00:07:47,700 --> 00:07:49,620
What's the meaning of this, Ryo-chan?

122
00:07:49,620 --> 00:07:50,980
There's nothing more to it.

123
00:07:50,980 --> 00:07:53,680
You guys have the wrong
idea about Chief Ohara.

124
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:56,800
I remodeled him into
the Chief's proper form.

125
00:07:56,800 --> 00:08:00,960
We really shouldn't have left
the senior officer alone back then.

126
00:08:01,520 --> 00:08:03,320
This isn't Chief Ohara at all.

127
00:08:03,320 --> 00:08:05,380
I've known him longer than you have.

128
00:08:05,380 --> 00:08:06,700
This one is the correct one.

129
00:08:06,700 --> 00:08:08,120
I already told you before.

130
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:10,800
That's because Ryo-chan
is always getting scolded.

131
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:13,720
So that's the Chief's true form.

132
00:08:14,240 --> 00:08:18,540
Even if we concede the hat, this is
still closer to the Chief's true image.

133
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:20,740
We can't give this as a present.

134
00:08:21,620 --> 00:08:22,520
Did you forget?

135
00:08:22,860 --> 00:08:27,020
This is Chief Ohara's 35th service anniversary gift,
remember?

136
00:08:27,820 --> 00:08:28,540
Right.

137
00:08:29,860 --> 00:08:32,620
Maybe we could use this as a chance
for him to reflect on himself.

138
00:08:33,440 --> 00:08:36,200
No one could be happy
getting something like this.

139
00:08:37,740 --> 00:08:39,960
I guess we'll have to have it remade.

140
00:08:40,800 --> 00:08:42,620
But we can't show it to the Chief, either.

141
00:08:43,040 --> 00:08:45,360
Hey! Then what do we do with this thing?

142
00:08:45,700 --> 00:08:48,260
Ryo-chan,
you take responsibility and get rid of it.

143
00:08:51,060 --> 00:08:54,560
Now that I think about it,
I wouldn't be happy getting it myself.

144
00:08:55,320 --> 00:08:56,900
Should we sell it somewhere?

145
00:09:02,780 --> 00:09:05,200
Well, how about 10,000?

146
00:09:05,660 --> 00:09:08,000
What? That's all it's worth?

147
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:10,340
Can't you throw in a little more?

148
00:09:10,340 --> 00:09:11,660
Then 20,000.

149
00:09:12,220 --> 00:09:14,220
Fine, I guess we'll settle on that.

150
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:16,580
What's this hand for?

151
00:09:16,580 --> 00:09:19,880
So you'll take this bronze statue
off my hands for 20,000, right?

152
00:09:19,880 --> 00:09:22,820
What are you talking about?
It's me who should be getting paid.

153
00:09:22,820 --> 00:09:27,640
What do you mean?
This shop buys antiques, doesn't it?

154
00:09:27,640 --> 00:09:29,580
Nobody could ever sell something like this.

155
00:09:29,580 --> 00:09:31,680
The 20,000 is a disposal fee.

156
00:09:31,680 --> 00:09:33,160
If you don't like it, take it back with you.

157
00:09:33,160 --> 00:09:35,800
Fine, forget it. I won't ask again.

158
00:09:37,180 --> 00:09:41,860
Even so,
there's nowhere else that'd take it.

159
00:09:43,520 --> 00:09:44,760
W-what is that?

160
00:09:45,140 --> 00:09:47,340
It's a present from me to the dorm.

161
00:09:47,340 --> 00:09:49,860
What are we supposed to do with that?

162
00:09:49,860 --> 00:09:52,680
It'd be perfect as cafeteria decor.

163
00:09:52,680 --> 00:09:54,560
Please don't do that.

164
00:09:54,560 --> 00:09:57,220
How about the bathroom?
I'll make it so hot water comes out of it.

165
00:09:57,220 --> 00:09:58,740
No way, it's creepy.

166
00:09:59,520 --> 00:10:02,600
Then let's display it at the
dorm entrance as a symbol statue.

167
00:10:02,600 --> 00:10:05,340
No, no!
Nobody will come near the place anymore.

168
00:10:05,800 --> 00:10:09,440
I didn't expect to be this hated.

169
00:10:11,820 --> 00:10:12,720
Oof, there we go.

170
00:10:13,940 --> 00:10:16,600
Can't be helped. I'll keep it in my room.

171
00:10:19,080 --> 00:10:22,020
Well, it's true it's not
exactly a pleasant thing to have.

172
00:10:23,840 --> 00:10:24,760
I'm hungry.

173
00:10:27,620 --> 00:10:30,217
Hey,

174
00:10:30,267 --> 00:10:33,305
What's the matter?

175
00:10:33,355 --> 00:10:35,120
Hey!

176
00:10:40,360 --> 00:10:43,280
It's just Chief's bronze bust.
Scared me for nothing.

177
00:10:44,680 --> 00:10:46,600
That's what happens when you
leave it somewhere like this.

178
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:49,520
Whoops, my ramen's going to get soggy.

179
00:10:51,980 --> 00:10:52,780
Thanks for the food.

180
00:10:54,920 --> 00:10:56,400
Was that a bit too early?

181
00:10:59,660 --> 00:11:02,800
I can't relax,
feeling like the Chief is watching me.

182
00:11:03,400 --> 00:11:04,860
Better turn it around.

183
00:11:05,800 --> 00:11:06,540
There, that's better.

184
00:11:10,640 --> 00:11:13,320
Now I'm even more worried
it'll suddenly turn around.

185
00:11:13,780 --> 00:11:15,320
Better blindfold it too.

186
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:18,200
How about this?

187
00:11:18,760 --> 00:11:19,620
Right then.

188
00:11:28,880 --> 00:11:30,880
Don't you give me that look.

189
00:11:34,660 --> 00:11:36,320
Now I can finally relax.

190
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:48,560
Where the hell should I put it?

191
00:11:50,500 --> 00:11:53,100
If I put it here, it'll be in a
blind spot from most of the room,

192
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:55,780
and it might even work as
a charm against evil spirits.

193
00:11:56,960 --> 00:12:04,260
Ryo-sama, I made too much nikujaga,
so would you like to eat with me?

194
00:12:04,260 --> 00:12:07,100
Oh my, what are you doing?

195
00:12:07,600 --> 00:12:10,000
It's just Maria. Don't scare me like that.

196
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:12,400
Actually, about that bust...

197
00:12:13,280 --> 00:12:14,100
The bust?

198
00:12:21,200 --> 00:12:23,240
I see. So that's how it is.

199
00:12:23,240 --> 00:12:23,927
Well then,

200
00:12:23,977 --> 00:12:27,520
I'll stay the night in
Ryo-sama's room tonight.

201
00:12:27,520 --> 00:12:30,400
Why would it come to that?

202
00:12:30,400 --> 00:12:30,974
Well,

203
00:12:31,024 --> 00:12:35,240
you don't want to be alone
with that bust, do you?

204
00:12:35,780 --> 00:12:36,940
W-well, yeah.

205
00:12:37,920 --> 00:12:42,480
I want to be with Ryo-sama, so isn't
this killing two birds with one stone?

206
00:12:43,080 --> 00:12:46,120
Tonight I'll be guarding Ryo-sama closely.

207
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:48,880
W-wait, wait,
that's probably not a good idea, is it?

208
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:52,280
Why not? What's the harm?

209
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:54,280
Hey, I'm a man, you know.

210
00:12:56,380 --> 00:12:58,960
Well, I guess that's better than
being alone with a bronze statue.

211
00:13:10,160 --> 00:13:10,780
Ryo-sama!

212
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:14,560
This is the third time now.

213
00:13:14,560 --> 00:13:16,380
This time, you slept right next to me.

214
00:13:16,380 --> 00:13:18,080
Shall we switch places?

215
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:19,080
Please.

216
00:13:21,620 --> 00:13:22,740
Good night.

217
00:13:23,600 --> 00:13:25,620
Finally I can sleep.

218
00:13:53,940 --> 00:13:58,040
Mm, have a safe trip, sir.

219
00:13:59,480 --> 00:14:04,920
I'm completely sleep-deprived,
and it's all thanks to this guy.

220
00:14:05,360 --> 00:14:07,280
If it comes to this, it's our last resort.

221
00:14:09,480 --> 00:14:10,900
Don't take it personally.

222
00:14:12,380 --> 00:14:13,220
Yah!

223
00:14:14,620 --> 00:14:15,020
Mm.

224
00:14:17,020 --> 00:14:20,540
Nya-nya-nya.

225
00:14:20,540 --> 00:14:23,240
Don't scare me like that.

226
00:14:27,980 --> 00:14:29,640
Hey, Ryotsu!

227
00:14:30,800 --> 00:14:32,560
How long are you going to keep sleeping?

228
00:14:32,560 --> 00:14:35,660
Whoa, I-I-I-I-I-I -

229
00:14:35,660 --> 00:14:38,260
What are you so surprised about?

230
00:14:38,260 --> 00:14:41,600
Eh so it's the real thing after all?

231
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:43,480
What are you talking about?

232
00:14:43,480 --> 00:14:45,240
N-n-n-nothing!

233
00:14:47,380 --> 00:14:50,320
You never know when a
major incident might happen.

234
00:14:50,320 --> 00:14:51,720
Yes, sir. Understood.

235
00:14:52,480 --> 00:14:54,700
This is terrible, a murder!

236
00:14:55,300 --> 00:14:55,940
What?

237
00:14:56,820 --> 00:14:59,060
There's a dismembered body
over at the storage area.

238
00:14:59,060 --> 00:14:59,880
Really?

239
00:15:00,500 --> 00:15:02,240
Ryotsu, head to the scene right away.

240
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:04,040
I'll contact the station.

241
00:15:04,040 --> 00:15:04,500
Understood.

242
00:15:06,900 --> 00:15:07,860
Hurry, hurry!

243
00:15:08,500 --> 00:15:09,360
It's over there.

244
00:15:09,360 --> 00:15:12,420
A corpse with a terrifying
face is inside a garbage bag.

245
00:15:12,420 --> 00:15:13,200
Look.

246
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:15,180
Where is this?

247
00:15:19,240 --> 00:15:20,160
Pretty amazing, right?

248
00:15:20,160 --> 00:15:21,960
Not amazing at all.

249
00:15:21,960 --> 00:15:23,360
That's a bronze statue.

250
00:15:23,360 --> 00:15:26,420
Damn, that cat must have done this.

251
00:15:27,940 --> 00:15:31,460
Ryotsu, where's the body?

252
00:15:32,400 --> 00:15:35,500
No, there was no body anywhere.

253
00:15:35,500 --> 00:15:36,220
What?

254
00:15:36,220 --> 00:15:38,440
It looks just like a corpse.

255
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:41,840
No, no, this guy just mistook something.

256
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:45,200
Looks like he mistook a mannequin
or something for a corpse.

257
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:46,400
See?

258
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:48,800
Then show me that mannequin.

259
00:15:48,800 --> 00:15:51,380
I have to write a report, just in case.

260
00:15:51,380 --> 00:15:54,420
I'll write the report myself.

261
00:15:54,420 --> 00:15:55,520
But...

262
00:15:55,520 --> 00:15:57,140
Leave it to me.

263
00:15:57,140 --> 00:16:00,280
Come to think of it,
this is just bulky trash, isn't it?

264
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:03,240
I'll dispose of this properly.

265
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:05,960
What on earth is wrong with him?

266
00:16:06,460 --> 00:16:06,860
There!

267
00:16:09,740 --> 00:16:10,720
And that's that.

268
00:16:11,220 --> 00:16:13,840
We'll never see each other again, I suppose.

269
00:16:22,500 --> 00:16:23,700
Welcome back.

270
00:16:23,700 --> 00:16:25,140
Grandma, I'm home.

271
00:16:25,920 --> 00:16:27,780
Ryo-san, you're in a good mood.

272
00:16:27,780 --> 00:16:28,600
Yeah, well.

273
00:16:29,400 --> 00:16:31,420
Now that that bronze bust is gone,

274
00:16:31,420 --> 00:16:33,860
I should finally be able
to get some sleep tonight.

275
00:16:40,660 --> 00:16:42,600
What's wrong, Ryo-san?

276
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:45,060
It was walking on its own.

277
00:16:45,060 --> 00:16:46,460
The bust...

278
00:16:46,460 --> 00:16:48,860
That? I'm the one who brought it.

279
00:16:48,860 --> 00:16:49,260
What?

280
00:16:49,720 --> 00:16:51,760
Well, during today's crackdown,

281
00:16:51,760 --> 00:16:53,860
I was chasing some bōsōzoku,

282
00:16:53,860 --> 00:16:56,260
and they ended up in a scrapyard.

283
00:16:57,160 --> 00:16:59,060
I lost track of them, though,

284
00:16:59,060 --> 00:17:00,280
but I found this.

285
00:17:01,020 --> 00:17:03,760
This bronze statue looks
just like Chief Ohara, right?

286
00:17:03,760 --> 00:17:06,340
I thought the senior officer
would get a big kick out of it,

287
00:17:06,340 --> 00:17:07,720
so I brought it back.

288
00:17:08,320 --> 00:17:08,760
I see.

289
00:17:09,260 --> 00:17:11,820
Why would you go and do
something so unnecessary?

290
00:17:22,040 --> 00:17:24,220
Don't you dare come back here again!

291
00:17:27,460 --> 00:17:29,960
This time it should be fine.

292
00:17:34,280 --> 00:17:35,900
I slept well.

293
00:17:37,860 --> 00:17:38,420
What?

294
00:17:40,580 --> 00:17:41,140
What?

295
00:17:41,320 --> 00:17:41,660
What?

296
00:17:41,660 --> 00:17:44,040
W-w-why is this here!

297
00:17:45,140 --> 00:17:47,640
Yeah, I left it there.

298
00:17:47,640 --> 00:17:48,494
Come on, Kankichi,

299
00:17:48,544 --> 00:17:51,800
weren't you two supposed to
be at the judo training camp?

300
00:17:52,260 --> 00:17:54,860
We just got back, actually.

301
00:17:54,860 --> 00:17:57,400
I was running along the beach this morning,

302
00:17:57,860 --> 00:17:59,960
and this had washed up on the shore.

303
00:18:00,840 --> 00:18:02,800
It looked just like Chief Ohara,

304
00:18:02,800 --> 00:18:04,920
so I figured it'd get a laugh,
and I left it there.

305
00:18:05,400 --> 00:18:07,020
It's not funny at all!

306
00:18:15,840 --> 00:18:18,620
I wonder what'll happen
to that bronze statue.

307
00:18:19,080 --> 00:18:24,480
It should lose its air somewhere in the
middle of the Pacific and sink into the sea.

308
00:18:24,480 --> 00:18:27,060
There's no way it'll come back now.

309
00:18:27,060 --> 00:18:29,100
Now I can finally relax.

310
00:18:32,800 --> 00:18:34,340
Ryotsu, are you in?

311
00:18:35,260 --> 00:18:38,880
What, it's you, you idiot?
I was just about to go to sleep.

312
00:18:38,880 --> 00:18:42,620
Don't say that.
I brought you a souvenir from overseas.

313
00:18:42,620 --> 00:18:47,100
Didn't you say you'd use your
vacation to go to America?

314
00:18:47,100 --> 00:18:50,280
So, what's the souvenir? Booze or food?

315
00:18:50,280 --> 00:18:52,080
It's quite a laughable item, this one.

316
00:18:52,080 --> 00:18:54,360
It fell from the sky right
before I came back to the country.

317
00:18:55,140 --> 00:18:55,900
From the sky?

318
00:18:55,900 --> 00:18:57,540
Don't be surprised when you see it.

319
00:19:06,340 --> 00:19:08,940
The Chief's bronze
statue isn't finished yet?

320
00:19:09,440 --> 00:19:12,560
The Metal 35-Year commendation
ceremony is tomorrow, though.

321
00:19:12,560 --> 00:19:17,420
I heard they'll finish it tonight and
take it straight to the venue tomorrow.

322
00:19:17,420 --> 00:19:21,860
They were devastated when they heard
the first one had to be redone, so...

323
00:19:21,860 --> 00:19:24,660
It must have taken them
a while to get over it.

324
00:19:24,660 --> 00:19:27,280
Speaking of which,
what happened to the first statue?

325
00:19:27,880 --> 00:19:29,240
Don't bring that up!

326
00:19:29,760 --> 00:19:31,600
Don't tell me you still have it?

327
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:34,640
Make sure Chief Ohara doesn't find out.

328
00:19:34,640 --> 00:19:37,248
That's right,
even a mild-mannered Chief Ohara,

329
00:19:37,298 --> 00:19:39,800
will definitely get angry
if he sees that statue.

330
00:19:39,800 --> 00:19:41,020
I know that!

331
00:19:41,620 --> 00:19:43,940
I want to get rid of it quickly too!

332
00:19:45,020 --> 00:19:46,500
Just bury it.

333
00:19:47,340 --> 00:19:47,900
Bury it?

334
00:19:48,280 --> 00:19:50,640
Yeah, somewhere out of sight, you know.

335
00:19:50,640 --> 00:19:51,960
Hey, how about the Aokigahara forest?

336
00:19:52,140 --> 00:19:55,820
The Fuji Aokigahara forest.
Nobody's going to find it there.

337
00:19:56,900 --> 00:19:57,740
Th-that's it!

338
00:20:05,060 --> 00:20:08,020
We should've just buried it from the start.

339
00:20:08,520 --> 00:20:10,660
If it's too shallow,
there's a risk it'll be found.

340
00:20:10,660 --> 00:20:12,540
Let's dig as deep as we can.

341
00:20:14,320 --> 00:20:15,680
If it's about this much,

342
00:20:20,640 --> 00:20:21,120
Ugh.

343
00:20:21,700 --> 00:20:22,460
Ugh...

344
00:20:22,460 --> 00:20:23,620
Phew...

345
00:20:23,620 --> 00:20:24,160
Phew...

346
00:20:24,160 --> 00:20:24,900
Phew...

347
00:20:24,900 --> 00:20:26,560
Hurry up.

348
00:20:26,560 --> 00:20:28,100
We almost got buried alive.

349
00:20:28,660 --> 00:20:30,360
If it had been buried right in
front of the bronze statue...

350
00:20:30,360 --> 00:20:32,500
No telling if it's murder or suicide.

351
00:20:33,440 --> 00:20:36,060
Okay, if we dig this much,
we're totally safe.

352
00:20:36,580 --> 00:20:37,320
This is bad.

353
00:20:43,380 --> 00:20:44,640
And that's it.

354
00:20:44,640 --> 00:20:46,380
Don't wander, just rest in peace.

355
00:20:57,940 --> 00:21:00,620
Chief Ohara's bronze statue is
apparently finished after all.

356
00:21:00,620 --> 00:21:02,880
Thank goodness, it made it just in time.

357
00:21:02,880 --> 00:21:04,980
Ryo-san's the one giving the speech, right?

358
00:21:04,980 --> 00:21:06,780
Leave it to me.

359
00:21:07,300 --> 00:21:09,040
You're really fired up.

360
00:21:09,860 --> 00:21:11,940
Well, I don't have any worries anymore.

361
00:21:17,140 --> 00:21:18,020
What's that?

362
00:21:22,360 --> 00:21:24,880
It's a hot spring!
A hot spring has welled up!

363
00:21:30,720 --> 00:21:37,320
We will now present the 35-year long-service
commendation to Senior Police Constable Daijirō Ohara.

364
00:21:39,960 --> 00:21:42,840
Hurry up, the ceremony's about to start!

365
00:21:42,840 --> 00:21:43,220
Yes.

366
00:21:44,720 --> 00:21:48,580
Certificate of Commendation: Daijirō Ohara.

367
00:21:48,580 --> 00:21:53,840
In recognition of your many years serving as
a model for all officers of Katsushika Station,

368
00:21:57,720 --> 00:21:58,600
Time's...

369
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:12,920
Next, we will present
the commemorative gift.

370
00:22:14,120 --> 00:22:15,580
Nakagawa, is it ready yet?

371
00:22:15,580 --> 00:22:16,400
Well, that's...

372
00:22:16,400 --> 00:22:17,380
It's here.

373
00:22:17,380 --> 00:22:18,740
Sorry to keep you waiting.

374
00:22:19,400 --> 00:22:20,240
Thank goodness.

375
00:22:20,240 --> 00:22:21,800
Just made it in time.

376
00:22:21,800 --> 00:22:24,120
Then, senior, I'm counting on you.

377
00:22:24,120 --> 00:22:25,120
Leave it to me.

378
00:22:25,120 --> 00:22:26,580
Sorry to keep you waiting.

379
00:22:26,580 --> 00:22:30,600
The presenter has had a long
association with Chief Ohara.

380
00:22:30,600 --> 00:22:33,140
Kankichi Ryotsu, Officer.

381
00:22:36,720 --> 00:22:41,100
Chief Ohara,
congratulations on your 35 years of service.

382
00:22:41,720 --> 00:22:42,160
Thank you.

383
00:22:43,300 --> 00:22:46,000
Looking back, right after I left school,

384
00:22:46,000 --> 00:22:48,180
I, who didn't know my right from my left,

385
00:22:48,180 --> 00:22:54,420
it was Chief Ohara who guided me,
sometimes gently and sometimes strictly.

386
00:22:55,180 --> 00:23:00,840
Out of youthful defiance,
I sometimes took a cheeky attitude.

387
00:23:00,840 --> 00:23:06,620
But deep in my heart, I looked up to
him as both a brother and a father.

388
00:23:10,620 --> 00:23:15,940
Chief Ohara combines strictness
with kindness and gentleness,

389
00:23:15,940 --> 00:23:18,440
truly a mirror for police officers.

390
00:23:18,440 --> 00:23:20,280
He is our ideal.

391
00:23:22,540 --> 00:23:27,540
That is why we have decided to present

392
00:23:27,540 --> 00:23:30,500
a statue of Chief Ohara,
the ideal police officer, as a gift.

393
00:23:30,980 --> 00:23:32,100
Please take a look.

394
00:23:32,100 --> 00:23:36,980
This is the image of Chief
Ohara that we idealize.

395
00:23:39,500 --> 00:23:40,592
W-what, w-what, w-what?

396
00:23:40,642 --> 00:23:43,880
Why is this here? We buried it.

397
00:23:45,300 --> 00:23:48,940
So that's your ideal, is it?

398
00:23:50,860 --> 00:23:57,340
I'll keep being your ideal,
and I'll be strict with you from now on.

399
00:23:57,900 --> 00:24:01,840
The real one is scarier after all.

400
00:24:15,100 --> 00:24:20,540
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling

401
00:24:21,740 --> 00:24:27,200
walking while looking back,
led by the hand of Gaaja

402
00:24:28,260 --> 00:24:34,380
that strange feeling I had back then

403
00:24:35,120 --> 00:24:39,600
So on the tiles of the arcade street

404
00:24:39,600 --> 00:24:45,400
I tried walking only on the black ones

405
00:24:47,920 --> 00:24:53,660
Everyone was a child once,
but they've all forgotten

406
00:24:54,640 --> 00:25:01,040
even the pompous-faced politicians
and the aunties with blue eyeshadow

407
00:25:01,040 --> 00:25:06,640
Go on, turn that corner

408
00:25:07,640 --> 00:25:11,800
you can meet everyone, everyone

409
00:25:12,360 --> 00:25:16,420
Over there is Kame-ari

410
00:25:17,240 --> 00:25:19,740
Surely Kame-ari

411
00:25:21,020 --> 00:25:25,040
Everyone, come on over to our town

412
00:25:25,860 --> 00:25:26,580
Thank you

413
00:25:30,480 --> 00:25:32,540
Scenes of cherished memories

414
00:25:32,540 --> 00:25:34,300
Even so, why should I have to

415
00:25:34,300 --> 00:25:36,720
tag along on Reiko's trip
to search for her memories,

416
00:25:36,720 --> 00:25:39,320
coming all the way out to this backwater?

417
00:25:39,320 --> 00:25:40,940
Whoa, Ōkuwagata!

418
00:25:40,940 --> 00:25:43,800
Alright, our trip is to find Kuwagata!

419
00:25:43,800 --> 00:25:47,500
Next time, Reiko's summer memories,
so look forward to it!

420
00:25:48,800 --> 00:25:51,000
That place is Kamearii.

421
00:25:52,080 --> 00:25:54,620
Well, surely it's Kamearii.

422
00:25:55,700 --> 00:25:59,340
Everyone, come on over to our town!

423
00:26:00,520 --> 00:26:00,920
Thank you.

424
00:26:02,540 --> 00:26:03,880
Thank you for watching.

